    /**  object (Required): object and {@see PaymentIntentInput}. One payment from a buyer, standalone or as a leg of an order. amount_money is the amount requested. Once the payment is authorized, authorized_money equals amount_money and splits into captured_money (collected), capturable_money (still on hold), and released_money (returned without being charged), so authorized_money always equals the sum of those three. Reconcile revenue from captured_money. object.add_on_fees (Optional): Array of {@see PaymentAddOnFeeInput}. Itemized invoice, subscription, and automatic tax fees collected with this payment. Available to the merchant only. Empty until fees settle or when no add-ons apply. Refunds do not return or revise these fees. Absent until Flint has determined and verified the fee. If Flint can't verify it when you read the payment intent, the field is omitted rather than shown unverified; read the payment intent again later. object.add_on_fees[] (Value): {@see PaymentAddOnFeeInput}. A Flint fee added to a payment intent, with the fee type and amount. object.amount_money (Required): {@see MoneyValueInput}. The amount requested from the buyer, including any tip_money. Capturing doesn't change it: after a partial capture it still shows the requested amount, and captured_money shows what was collected. On a standalone payment intent, PATCH can change it only before the first confirmation attempt. Monetary amount represented as integer minor units plus an ISO 4217 currency code. object.authorization_expires_at (Optional): string. Deadline to capture a manual-capture hold. The authorization lapses at this time, and a capture attempted after it fails even if status is still requires_capture. Set when the hold is placed. Format: date-time. object.authorized_at (Optional): string. When the processor authorized the payment. Absent until then. Format: date-time. object.authorized_money (Optional): {@see MoneyValueInput}. The amount the processor authorized. It always equals amount_money and doesn't change once set. Absent until the payment is authorized, and on payments canceled before authorization. Monetary amount represented as integer minor units plus an ISO 4217 currency code. object.cancellation_reason (Optional): string. Flint-normalized reason the payment intent was canceled. Present only while status is canceled. Unknown processor values are returned as payment_canceled. Value enum: "requested_by_customer", "duplicate", "fraudulent", "abandoned", "invoice_payment_failed", "invoice_voided", "order_closed", "payment_canceled". object.capturable_money (Optional): {@see MoneyValueInput}. The part of the authorization you can still capture. Positive only while status is requires_capture, and zero after you capture or cancel or the authorization expires. The authorization lapses at authorization_expires_at, and a capture attempted after that fails even if this is positive. Absent until the payment is authorized. Monetary amount represented as integer minor units plus an ISO 4217 currency code. object.capture_method (Optional): string. When money is collected. Defaults to automatic. Value enum: "automatic", "manual". object.captured_at (Optional): string. When money was captured. For automatic capture, this is when the payment succeeded. Absent until capture. Format: date-time. object.captured_money (Optional): {@see MoneyValueInput}. The amount collected from the buyer. Reconcile revenue and print receipts from this amount, not amount_money. Zero while a hold is open, and positive whenever status is succeeded. processing_fee_money, merchant_net_money, and refunds are based on it. Absent until the payment is authorized. Monetary amount represented as integer minor units plus an ISO 4217 currency code. object.checkout_session_id (Optional): string. Flint checkout session ID associated with this payment, when present. object.created_at (Optional): string. RFC3339 timestamp. Format: date-time. object.customer (Optional): {@see ExpandedCustomerSummaryInput} or null. The linked customer. Returned only with expand=customer. Present only when `expand` includes `customer`; `null` when expanded and there is no related customer. object.customer.anyOf[1] (Value): {@see ExpandedCustomerSummaryInput}. A customer's summary fields, returned in place of a customer ID when the customer is expanded. object.customer.anyOf[2] (Value): null. object.customer_id (Optional): string. Customer linked to this payment intent. object.dispute_status (Optional): string. Dispute state of this payment. none means no dispute or inquiry is open or recorded. The inquiry_ values track an issuer inquiry or early warning that isn't a chargeback. Read the dispute with GET /v1/disputes for its deadline and evidence. Value enum: "none", "inquiry_needs_response", "inquiry_under_review", "inquiry_closed", "needs_response", "under_review", "won", "lost", "prevented", "other". object.external_reference_id (Optional): string or null. Caller-owned identifier for this resource in an external system. minLength: 1. maxLength: 255. object.fulfillment_hold (Optional): {@see PaymentFulfillmentHoldInput}. Present when a payment provider asked Flint to pause fulfillment for this payment. While its status is active, open fulfillments on the order are on hold with reason payment_review. payment_intent.fulfillment_hold_updated is sent when the hold starts and when it lifts. A hold on fulfillment tied to a payment, with the reason, the action required, and whether the hold is active or released. object.invoice (Optional): {@see ExpandedInvoiceSummaryInput} or null. The linked invoice. Returned only with expand=invoice. Present only when `expand` includes `invoice`; `null` when expanded and there is no related invoice. object.invoice.anyOf[1] (Value): {@see ExpandedInvoiceSummaryInput}. An invoice's summary fields, including status, due date, and paid, outstanding, and refunded amounts, returned when the invoice is expanded. object.invoice.anyOf[2] (Value): null. object.invoice_id (Optional): string. Invoice this payment intent collects, when it pays an invoice. object.last_payment_error (Required): {@see PaymentErrorSummaryInput} or null. Most recent payment error. Null when no payment error is recorded. object.last_payment_error.anyOf[1] (Value): {@see PaymentErrorSummaryInput}. A summary of why a payment attempt failed, with a normalized error code, a message, the failure time, and remediation. object.last_payment_error.anyOf[2] (Value): null. object.merchant_id (Optional): string. Merchant that owns this payment intent. object.merchant_net_money (Optional): {@see MoneyValueInput}. Captured amount minus processing_fee_money and every amount in add_on_fees. Later merchant assessments and credits are separate balance effects. Absent until Flint has determined and verified the fee. If Flint can't verify it when you read the payment intent, the field is omitted rather than shown unverified; read the payment intent again later. Monetary amount represented as integer minor units plus an ISO 4217 currency code. object.metadata (Required): {@see MetadataMapInput}. Caller-owned metadata. Keys starting with flint_ are reserved for Flint and aren't returned. Caller-owned key-value data stored on a resource. Keys starting with flint_ are reserved for Flint and are not returned. Writes follow the limits on MetadataInput and MetadataPatchInput; maps written before those limits may not satisfy them. object.order (Optional): {@see ExpandedOrderSummaryInput} or null. The linked order. Returned only with expand=order. Present only when `expand` includes `order`; `null` when expanded and there is no related order. object.order.anyOf[1] (Value): {@see ExpandedOrderSummaryInput}. An order's summary fields, including status, payment and refund status, and pricing and settlement amounts, returned when the order is expanded. object.order.anyOf[2] (Value): null. object.order_id (Optional): string. Order this payment intent belongs to. Create it through the order and confirm it with POST /v1/orders/{order_id}/pay. Capture and cancel use POST /v1/payment-intents/{payment_intent_id}/capture or /cancel for every payment intent. Order-owned intents accept PATCH for metadata and external_reference_id. object.payment_flow (Required): string. How the payment was started. Fixed when the payment intent is created. Value enum: "checkout", "payment_link", "invoice", "subscription_initial", "subscription_renewal", "virtual_terminal", "api". object.payment_intent_id (Required): string. Flint payment intent ID. object.payment_options (Required): Array of string. Payment options the buyer can use for this payment. [] enum: "card", "apple_pay", "google_pay", "affirm", "ach_debit". object.payment_options[] (Value): string.  Value enum: "card", "apple_pay", "google_pay", "affirm", "ach_debit". object.payment_source (Optional): {@see PaymentSourceSummaryInput}. Summary of the card or bank account used for the payment. Absent until a payment source is attached. A summary of the payment source used for a payment, by funding-method family, with card or bank account display details. object.processing_fee_money (Optional): {@see MoneyValueInput}. Flint's all-in processing fee for this payment. It is the complete price Flint charges to process the payment, never a provider cost passed through. The fee is final once the card payment is captured or the ACH payment succeeds; canceled payments and failures before success have none. Invoice, subscription, and automatic tax fees are itemized separately in add_on_fees. Your net for the payment is captured_money minus this fee and the add-on fees. Refunds do not return or revise it. Absent until Flint has determined and verified the fee. If Flint can't verify it when you read the payment intent, the field is omitted rather than shown unverified; read the payment intent again later. Monetary amount represented as integer minor units plus an ISO 4217 currency code. object.receipt_email (Optional): string or null. Email address for this payment's receipt. When it isn't set, Flint uses the customer's email. Format: email. maxLength: 255. object.refund_status (Optional): string. How much of captured_money has been refunded, including value issued as store credit, based on refunded_money. Value enum: "none", "partially_refunded", "refunded". object.refunded_money (Optional): {@see MoneyValueInput}. Total refunded against captured_money, including value issued as store credit and processor refunds still pending. Failed and canceled refunds aren't counted. Zero when nothing has been refunded. Monetary amount represented as integer minor units plus an ISO 4217 currency code. object.released_money (Optional): {@see MoneyValueInput}. The part of the authorization returned to the buyer without being charged: the uncaptured remainder after a partial capture, or the whole authorization after a cancellation or expiry. It was never collected, so it needs no refund and can't be captured later. Absent until the payment is authorized. Monetary amount represented as integer minor units plus an ISO 4217 currency code. object.return_id (Optional): string. Flint return ID associated with this payment, when present. object.risk (Optional): {@see PaymentRiskInput} or null. Risk assessment. Always present with merchant credentials; null when no risk assessment is available. Omitted with the checkout credential. object.risk.anyOf[1] (Value): {@see PaymentRiskInput}. The risk assessment for a payment intent, with its risk level, score, outcome, and any matched rule or review. object.risk.anyOf[2] (Value): null. object.selected_payment_option (Optional): string. The payment option the most recent confirmation used. Absent until the payment intent is first confirmed. object.status (Required): string. Lifecycle status. requires_payment_method covers both a new payment intent and one whose last attempt failed, so read last_payment_error with it. succeeded, canceled, and expired are final. Refunds and disputes never change status. Value enum: "requires_payment_method", "requires_confirmation", "requires_action", "processing", "requires_capture", "canceled", "succeeded", "expired". object.support_reference (Required): string. Opaque payment reference to share with merchant support. Do not parse its format. object.supported_actions (Required): Array of string. Actions the payment intent's current state accepts, each a POST to /v1/payment-intents/{payment_intent_id}/{action}. An action that isn't listed returns 409 ACTION_NOT_ALLOWED. A listed action can still be refused because of something outside the payment intent: an open risk review, an order payment attempt that is using this payment, a closed order, or the merchant's account. An order-owned payment intent never lists confirm; pay it with POST /v1/orders/{order_id}/pay. The list changes only when the payment intent changes. Always empty for buyer credentials. New actions may be added. [] enum: "confirm", "capture", "cancel". object.supported_actions[] (Value): string.  Value enum: "confirm", "capture", "cancel". object.tip_money (Optional): {@see MoneyValueInput} or null. Portion of amount_money that is a tip. Uses amount_money's currency and is at most amount_money. object.tip_money.anyOf[1] (Value): {@see MoneyValueInput}. Monetary amount represented as integer minor units plus an ISO 4217 currency code. object.tip_money.anyOf[2] (Value): null. object.transaction_purpose (Optional): string. Why a bank debit is taken. Set only when payment_options includes ach_debit, and fixed once the payment intent exists. Value enum: "goods", "services", "other". object.updated_at (Optional): string. RFC3339 timestamp. Format: date-time. object.version (Required): integer. Persisted version of this resource's owned state. Expanded resources and external observations can change independently. Format: uint64. minimum: 1.
